  ["Role", "Their one number", "Why this one"],
  [
    ["Owner", "Weekly revenue versus target", "The only number that aggregates everything else. Everyone else's number rolls into it."],
    ["Front desk", "Inquiries booked today", "The only metric they fully control. It is also the cheapest revenue in the building."],
    ["Provider or injector", "Revenue per booked hour", "Captures mix, pricing, and rebooking in one figure. It rewards judgment rather than volume."],
    ["Consultant or coordinator", "Consult conversion rate", "The clearest measure of the highest-leverage conversation in the practice."],
    ["Manager", "Net new memberships", "Recurring revenue is the only metric that compounds while everyone sleeps."]
  ],
  [1600, 2500, 5260]
));
body.push(P("Five people, five numbers. Not one dashboard with forty metrics that everybody nods at and nobody owns.", { italics: true }));

body.push(H2("How to present goals on Monday without losing the room"));
body.push(numbered("Present the weekly number, never the annual one. Two point four million is a threat. Forty-eight thousand is a plan."));
